---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why OpenBench exists and who builds it."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-700">About OpenBench</h1>
    <div class="prose-ob mt-6 space-y-4 text-[var(--ob-ink)]/85">
      <p>
        OpenBench is a small, growing set of free, open-source utilities for
        test and automation engineers — built by someone who uses tools like
        these professionally, on a real bench, every week.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commercial tools in this space work fine, but they're closed-source
        and licensed per seat, which is real friction for something you
        might use for twenty minutes before a site visit. OpenBench tools
        are free to download, free to audit, and released under the MIT
        license.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project is funded by donations and, eventually, an optional paid
        tier for teams that need remote or cloud features the free,
        local-only tools don't cover. The core tools themselves stay free —
        that's not changing.
      </p>
      <p>
        OpenBench is currently a side project, built in spare hours around a
        full-time role in test, measurement, and automation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
